# Medora broker ACL (mqtt-topics.md v1.2). Username = device id for bedside units.
# Anonymous clients are rejected in mosquitto.conf; a topic not listed here is denied.

# Backend (worker + API): reads what devices send, writes what devices receive, owns ward/internal/#.
user ward-backend
topic read hospital/device/+/vitals
topic read hospital/device/+/events
topic read hospital/device/+/status
topic write hospital/device/+/schedule
topic write hospital/device/+/command
topic readwrite ward/internal/#

# Every other user is a bedside unit / simulator; %u is its device id, so it only sees its own topics.
# The last-will is on status (write). The unit also reads its own events to see dose_taken.
pattern write hospital/device/%u/vitals
pattern write hospital/device/%u/status
pattern readwrite hospital/device/%u/events
pattern read hospital/device/%u/schedule
pattern read hospital/device/%u/command
